<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Władysław II of Płock</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1448–1462</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Władysław II of Płock was a Piast duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a> who ruled the lands of Płock, Rawa, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gostynin">Gostynin</a> and neighbouring districts jointly with his elder brother Siemowit VI from 1455. Both brothers died young in early 1462, Władysław in February, without heirs. Their deaths allowed King Casimir IV to annex Rawa and Gostynin to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a>, an important step towards the absorption of Masovia.</p></div>
